    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Gets predictions for image detection. It compares confidence scores for each of the instance categories."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f0NjYKoD_dET"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def filter_boxes(predictions, conf_thresh):\n",
        "\n",
        "    #initialize empty dictionary/lists to store the generated data\n",
        "    dictionary = {}\n",
        "    boxes_list = []\n",
        "    scores_list = []\n",
        "    labels_list = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i in range(len(predictions[0][\"boxes\"])):\n",
        "        score = predictions[0][\"scores\"][i]     #confidence score - how sure the yolo model is that an object is correcty classified.\n",
        "        if score >= conf_thresh:\n",
        "            boxes_list.append(predictions[0][\"boxes\"][i])\n",
        "            scores_list.append(predictions[0][\"scores\"][[i]])\n",
        "            labels_list.append(predictions[0][\"labels\"][[i]])\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Check if boxes_list is empty BEFORE stacking on top of image\n",
        "    if boxes_list:\n",
        "        dictionary[\"boxes\"] = np.vstack(boxes_list)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        dictionary[\"boxes\"] = np.empty((0, 4))  # Return an empty array with the correct shape\n",
        "\n",
        "    if scores_list:\n",
        "        dictionary[\"scores\"] = np.hstack(scores_list)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        dictionary[\"scores\"] = np.empty((0,))\n",
        "\n",
        "    if labels_list:\n",
        "        dictionary[\"labels\"] = np.hstack(labels_list)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        dictionary[\"labels\"] = np.empty((0,))\n",
        "\n",
        "    y = [dictionary]\n",
        "\n",
        "    return y\n",
        "\n",
        "y = [filter_boxes([t], 0.8)[0] for t in dets]"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1b3dysJJ9XUQ"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#Attack 1: A Basic Adversarial Patch Attack:\n",
        "This manually applies a patch directly on top of the image set. It's helpful to walk through the process and see what goes on behind the scenes. This kind of attack basically aims to simply NOT classify certain objects in the image, rather than perceive them as something else."
