    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#Attack 2: RobustPatch Attack\n",
        "This attack also utilizes a patch, but performs multiple iterations on an image to eventually misclassify objects. It starts with its own randomly generated patch, that it can update, so there's no need to use the one from earlier. This is much more powerful, and can be much more disruptive than the basic paste-and-go attack from earlier. The end goal is a *misclassification* of objects within an image."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UY81PlAL_1jG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "*This might take 20-30 minutes to run, but it serves as an example of what patch attacks are capable of. To save time, only the first image in the set is being targeted.*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qab4QjSFdO72"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from art.attacks.evasion import RobustDPatch\n",
        "\n",
        "x = image_set[:-1]\n",
        "y = [y[-1] for i in range(len(image_set[:-1]))]\n",
        "\n",
        "#attack settings\n",
        "#if you have the time, can mess with these to understand how they contribute to the attack.\n",
        "attack = RobustDPatch(\n",
        "    detector,\n",
        "    patch_shape=(3, 200, 200),\n",
        "    patch_location=(200, 200),\n",
        "    crop_range=[0,0],\n",
        "    brightness_range=[0.9, 1.1],\n",
        "    rotation_weights=[1, 0, 0, 0],\n",
        "    sample_size=1,\n",
        "    learning_rate=2.0,\n",
        "    max_iter=10,\n",
        "    batch_size=1,\n",
        "    verbose=False,\n",
        "    targeted=True #this tailors the patch to the specific image it's to be applied on. Requires more computational power, but yields better results.\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "loss_history = []\n",
        "#TODO - if you have the time, compare different iterations with classification results.\n",
        "#Anything over 30 is not recommended due to timing constraints, but this is a project you can have running in the background.\n",
        "for i in tqdm(range(15)):\n",
        "    patch = attack.generate(x, y)\n"   #if you're running an untargeted attack, get rid of the y parameter, as it's no longer needed to direct the attack,
        "    patched_images = attack.apply_patch(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "    loss_components, _ = detector._get_losses(patched_images, dets[:-1])\n",
        "    losses = {}\n",
        "    for loss in loss_components.keys():\n",
        "        if 'loss' in loss:\n",
        "            losses[loss] = loss_components[loss].item()\n",
        "    loss_history.append(losses)\n",
        "\n",
        "#every 5 iterations, check to see how predictions are affected.\n",
        "    if i%5==0:\n",
        "        _y = detector.predict(patched_images)\n",
        "        preds = extract_predictions(_y[0], 0.5)\n",
        "        im = (patched_images[0].transpose(1,2,0)).astype(np.uint8)\n",
        "        plot_image_with_boxes(img=im.astype(np.uint8).copy(), boxes=preds[1], pred_cls=preds[0], title=f\"Detection [iter: {i}]\")\n",
        "\n",
        "_y = detector.predict(patched_images)\n",
        "preds = extract_predictions(_y[0], 0.5)\n",
        "im = (patched_images[0].transpose(1,2,0)).astype(np.uint8)\n",
        "plot_image_with_boxes(img=im.astype(np.uint8).copy(), boxes=preds[1], pred_cls=preds[0], title=f\"Detection [final]\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5J6CsPbc9XXY"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Visualizes the various losses from the Robust Patch Attack:\\\n",
        "*As iterations increase, there's a loss of accuracy in the classifications*"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KOP6no5xeFtj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "%matplotlib inline\n",
        "losses = pd.DataFrame(loss_history)\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(nrows=1,ncols=3,figsize=(12,3))\n",
        "losses.loss_cls.plot(ylabel='loss', ax = axes[0], subplots=True, color='g')\n",
        "losses.loss_box.plot(xlabel='epoch', ax = axes[1],subplots=True, color='royalblue')\n",
        "losses.loss_obj.plot( ax = axes[2],subplots=True, color='orange')\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].set_title('Classification Loss')\n",
        "axes[1].set_title('Box Loss')\n",
        "axes[2].set_title('Objectness Loss')\n",
        "fig.tight_layout()"
